WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.440
If you've been wondering where&nbsp;
two of the most famous sisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.320
in the world have been since they&nbsp;
stopped making movies together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.856
you're probably not alone. Here's why you don't&nbsp;
hear very much about the Olsen twins anymore.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.120
If you grew up watching Full House, you're&nbsp;
definitely familiar with the Olsen twins'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.203
first big role, but you might not realize just&nbsp;
how young they were when they got started.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.203 --> 00:00:22.960
After both Mary-Kate and Ashley were cast&nbsp;
to play the family's most adorable member,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.480
Michelle, at just six months&nbsp;
old, they became stars thanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:30.560
to the show's enduring popularity and&nbsp;
overwhelming affection for the character.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.991
"I've been on Full House forever."

00:00:36.991 --> 00:00:39.840
However, since the twins started&nbsp;
so young, they didn't really get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.000
to choose their careers. Full House was a&nbsp;
great opportunity for Mary-Kate and Ashley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.614
but it makes sense that they eventually&nbsp;
retired in favor of other pursuits.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.760
Whether or not Mary-Kate and Ashley got the&nbsp;
chance to choose their childhood profession,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.920
there's no denying that their tenure&nbsp;
as actresses was insanely lucrative.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.640
"My favorite thing is eating a cake."

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:02.880
After they got older, Mary-Kate and Ashley&nbsp;
launched Dualstar Entertainment, spawning a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.000
fan club that served as a subscription site and as&nbsp;
the backbone to the twins' growing media empire.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.520
In 2007, the Olsens even joined&nbsp;
powerhouses like talk show host&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.280
Oprah Winfrey on the Forbes ranking of&nbsp;
the wealthiest women in entertainment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.480
with the publication estimating their net wealth&nbsp;
at $100 million and noting that Dualstar sold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:25.680
quote, "$1 billion worth of merchandise&nbsp;
worldwide in a year–everything from videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.160
to hair-care products." At the time, the twins&nbsp;
were just 20 years old. Making their fortune&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.310
at a seriously young age enabled them to&nbsp;
step out of the limelight fairly early.

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.440
It might seem a little crazy that Mary-Kate and&nbsp;
Ashley were raking in literal billions before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:43.280
they could legally drink, but when you consider&nbsp;
just how hard the twins worked throughout their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.160
acting career, you'll understand why. After Full&nbsp;
House, the two embarked on a series of features,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.400
television films, and direct-to-video&nbsp;
releases throughout the 1990s. All told,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.040
the twins appeared in 27&nbsp;
projects between 1992 and 2004.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.840
However, 2004 brought an end to their&nbsp;
joint acting careers with New York Minute,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.440
their second theatrical release.&nbsp;
Ultimately, the film performed poorly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.720
both critically and commercially -&nbsp;
having one of the lowest openings of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.179
all time - which wasn't exactly a favorable&nbsp;
conclusion to the girls' acting career.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.160
The Olsens were two of the most famous young&nbsp;
women in the world throughout their childhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.000
and adolescence. However, it should come as&nbsp;
no surprise that this fame came with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:26.480
serious drawbacks - specifically,&nbsp;
some very gross objectification.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.920
In June of 2019, writer Yomi Adegoke penned&nbsp;
a piece about men in dark corners of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.320
internet who, quote, "count down" until&nbsp;
young women turn 18 and become "legal,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.800
mentioning the Olsen twins as an example.&nbsp;
Mary-Kate and Ashley had grown up on camera,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.520
from their casting in Full House at just&nbsp;
six months old onward. Adegoke wrote,

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:47.760
"Men patiently waiting until they hit puberty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.710
and their fantasies made the switch from&nbsp;
perverse to pedestrian, made me feel queasy."

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.200
Adegoke spends the rest of her essay detailing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:59.040
seriously damaging implications of this&nbsp;
upsetting trend, which was potentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.179
harmful to the Olsens and may have played&nbsp;
a role in their decision to leave acting.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:08.080
In the years since New York Minute flopped at&nbsp;
the box office, the Olsens have found solace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.720
and success in an entirely new venture&nbsp;
in the world of high fashion. In 2006,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.280
the twins launched The Row. The brand was the&nbsp;
result of Ashley's goal to create the perfect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.960
white t-shirt. However, the two preferred&nbsp;
to let the clothes speak for themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.267
and didn't even do a public interview about&nbsp;
The Row for several years after its debut.

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:32.524
"It's not a trend-based brand. It's really about&nbsp;
what these women want to be wearing every day."

00:03:32.524 --> 00:03:37.040
The Row - which the Olsens still own and manage&nbsp;
alongside lines like Elizabeth &amp; James, a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:42.720
concept named for their siblings - has won several&nbsp;
awards. It even took home the highest honor of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:47.520
Council of the Fashion Designers of America, the&nbsp;
Womenswear Designer of the Year Award, two years&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:52.240
in a row. In 2018, the Olsens announced that&nbsp;
the Row would launch a menswear line, complete&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:57.151
with knits, suits, and denim. Why return to acting&nbsp;
when you've got a successful fashion collection?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:02.160
In the absence of their acting career, both&nbsp;
Mary-Kate and Ashley have been pretty focused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:06.800
on becoming fashion mavens. However, throughout&nbsp;
the years, Mary-Kate has struck out on her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.995
to debut a talent that she doesn't seem&nbsp;
to share with her twin: horseback riding.

00:04:10.995 --> 00:04:14.800
According to PopSugar, Mary-Kate&nbsp;
was spotted in September of 2016&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.120
competing in the annual American Gold Cup,&nbsp;
which is held at the Old Salem Farm in New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:23.280
York. The publication reported that Mary-Kate&nbsp;
rode three different horses during the event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:27.600
which is considered one of the most renowned&nbsp;
show jumping events in the world. By that point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.920
Mary-Kate had been riding horses competitively&nbsp;
for three years and had been photographed riding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:36.240
recreationally in places like the Hamptons.&nbsp;
It seems like this hobby holds more interest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:40.657
for Mary-Kate than acting, and she's clearly&nbsp;
talented if she made it into this famous event.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.800
Though it might seem like the Olsens&nbsp;
do just about everything together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.240
you might not realize that after&nbsp;
one twin stopped acting entirely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:52.560
the other stayed on screen for just a little&nbsp;
while longer. After Ashley stopped acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:58.000
Mary-Kate continued, appearing in projects&nbsp;
like the critically panned 2011 film Beastly.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.960
However, in 2012, the twins told Elle UK that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.000
were out of the game for good.&nbsp;
As Mary-Kate told the magazine,

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.939
"It just felt right to move&nbsp;
away [from the spotlight]."

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.310
Meanwhile, Ashley said,

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.920
"I don't have to be a pretty face. I've&nbsp;
done that, but now it's important and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.445
liberating to be on the other side of the lens. I&nbsp;
don't like to be the center of attention anymore."

00:05:16.445 --> 00:05:18.560
She added that she's still&nbsp;
interested in Hollywood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:22.240
but that if she ever returned, it wouldn't&nbsp;
be as an actress. The two clearly found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:25.440
their bliss elsewhere — and with&nbsp;
each other. Mary-Kate told Elle,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.800
"Nothing would ever split us up.&nbsp;
Separate side projects are one thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.320
but we work better as a team."

